### Figma preview chrome — do not implement

On **all** v0.3 screens, **ignore** device status-bar / system-chrome layers from Figma. They exist only for design preview, not in the app — **iPhone and Android**.

| Layer | Figma (preview only) |
|-------|----------------------|
| iPhone upper status bar (time, signal, battery) | `node-id=12822-3572` |
| iPhone lower home indicator | `node-id=12822-3639` |
| Android upper status bar | `Android Phone`, `iPhone-status-bar(upper)` variants, `12697:38980` et al. |
| Android lower navigation / home bar | Android lower system chrome in `get_design_context` |

- Do **not** render `IPhoneStatusBarUpper`, `iPhone-status-bar(lower)`, `Android Phone`, or similar components from `get_design_context`.
- Do **not** reserve top/bottom padding to match those preview frames (no offset for 44px / 32px Figma chrome).
- **Full-screen layout:** implement on the full **375×812** mobile artboard and let the funnel **fill the device viewport** (`FunnelViewport`, `fixed inset-0`). Spread heroes, video, and backgrounds edge-to-edge; do not shrink the canvas to sit “between” status bars.
- `env(safe-area-inset-*)` is for real notches/home indicators on physical devices only — not for mimicking Figma preview chrome.
- Figma absolute Y/X coordinates assume the **full 812px** height; use them as-is (no subtracting status-bar height).
- **Short viewports:** do not height-shrink the funnel to fit — use `scaleMode="scroll"` and vertical scroll. See `.cursor/rules/v03-small-viewports.mdc`.

